  "highestRiskFindings": [
    "The exact-bound revision-fixture audit proves that 122 of 240 flawed fixtures violate the exhaustive one-code contract: 102 instantiate A plus B or another independent error, 18 instantiate B or an unlisted error without A, and 2 instantiate neither A nor B. Every successor must make its revision fixture instantiate common error A exactly and only.",
    "ED:001, ED:020, ED:031, ED:044, ED:045, ED:066, and ED:073 are early B-or-unlisted-without-A fixtures; ED:163 and ED:164 are late neither-or-unlisted fixtures; all are explicit rubric successors.",
    "ED:084, ED:087, ED:088, ED:093, ED:107, ED:115, ED:127, ED:143, ED:146, ED:149, and ED:155 have milestones that require work not requested by the current statement.",
    "ED:087, ED:107, ED:109, ED:115, and ED:154 retain instructionally intended richer requests and therefore require matching canonical-solution and mirrored positive-fixture additions.",
    "ED:122 removes unnecessary pre-supplied answer formulas from the statement and therefore also requires dependent hint and milestone repairs.",
    "ED:099 names dielectric surface pressure although the task and solution concern conductor traction in vacuum.",
    "ED:117 must explicitly require both dielectric materials so the claimed interior optimum is not defeated by the single-material endpoint.",
    "ED:130 must recognize midpoint-circle symmetry for the isolated segment, state that a steady open segment is impossible, and account for the generally symmetry-breaking return path.",
    "ED:109, ED:120, and ED:150 have insufficient or mixed sign and normal conventions.",
    "ED:159 must treat g_sat = g_min as the saturation threshold, not as an unsaturated branch.",
    "ED:217 must replace reactive time-domain flux language and its stale reactive-flux skill identifier; analogous synthetic audit or ledger skill identifiers in affected successors require ordinary disciplinary names.",
    "ED:238 calls a scalar energy accounting relation a vector energy ledger.",
    "ED:167 has a malformed permitted formula; ED:205 confuses scalar and vector wave number notation; ED:206 uses A/B shorthand that collides with magnetic-field notation and requires both version successors.",
    "Every /solution edit also changes canonicalSolution and the mirrored positive fixture, so it is problem-and-rubric scoped; the explicit 11/109/47 per-ID map is authoritative and must not be weakened to count-only validation."
  ],
